research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral.md-344-  "rationale": "Semmes, Sections 8.1.2–8.1.3, defines finite-dimensional vector Riemann–Stieltjes integrals componentwise, identifies the ordinary Riemann case by alpha(t)=t, and states both integrability of the norm and the inequality N(integral f) <= integral N(f), including the Riemann-integrable rather than merely continuous setting. The item specializes to the Euclidean norm, makes the a <= b/oriented-integral boundary explicit, and proves the result locally using the library’s componentwise Darboux integral and scalar theorem interfaces. The supplied numbered argument was audited as a local proof rather than a transcription or identifiable adaptation of a source proof.",
